===== orchestration/README.md =====
# Orchestration environment

Install the isolated CrewAI control-layer dependencies with `uv` from the
repository root:

```bash
uv venv --python 3.12 .venv-orchestration
uv pip sync --python .venv-orchestration/bin/python orchestration/requirements.txt
```

Run the orchestration tests with the same interpreter:

```bash
.venv-orchestration/bin/python -m pytest -q
```

The root `requirements.txt` is historical and is intentionally unchanged.

Run one or more explicit phases as before:

```bash
python -m orchestration.main --phase "Phase 5" --max-attempts 3
```

Or resume automatically from the first structurally valid incomplete checkpoint:

```bash
python -m orchestration.main --auto --max-attempts 3
```

Auto mode requires a clean worktree before a new phase, never reruns a valid PASS
checkpoint, stops on permission or Git-safety concerns, creates local phase
commits only after independent PASS, and never pushes or deploys.
===== orchestration/config/agents.yaml =====
supervisor:
  role: Supervisor
  goal: Route each approved project phase to the correct specialist and enforce every safety and validation gate.
  responsibilities:
    - Read the repository governance documents before routing work.
    - Select the specialist profile from the deterministic phase map.
    - Stop when validation is malformed or the retry limit is exhausted.
    - Advance only after an independent validator returns PASS.

data_agent:
  role: Data Agent
  goal: Implement data validation, preprocessing, EDA, and data-quality phases without leakage.
  responsibilities:
    - Preserve chronological ordering and source data.
    - Report missing, duplicate, invalid, and suspicious observations.
    - Do not start external or Indian-city data acquisition.

feature_agent:
  role: Feature Agent
  goal: Implement past-only feature engineering and training-only feature selection.
  responsibilities:
    - Shift lag and rolling inputs so they cannot observe the prediction target.
    - Keep feature selection isolated from validation and locked test data.

ml_agent:
  role: ML Agent
  goal: Implement traditional ML and validation-only optimization experiments.
  responsibilities:
    - Compare simple baselines before claiming improvement.
    - Fit preprocessing only on training data.
    - Use chronological holdouts and time-aware cross-validation.

timeseries_agent:
  role: Time-Series Agent
  goal: Implement classical and neural time-series baselines with chronological evaluation.
  responsibilities:
    - Preserve temporal causality in model inputs and evaluation.
    - Use GPU only when supported and useful.

transformer_agent:
  role: Transformer Agent
  goal: Evaluate PatchTST and approved transformer candidates without assuming superiority.
  responsibilities:
    - Keep locked test data isolated from tuning and selection.
    - Preserve configurations, seeds, predictions, metrics, and logs.

ui_agent:
  role: UI Agent
  goal: Implement and verify the Streamlit interface and result presentation.
  responsibilities:
    - Use preserved experiment artifacts rather than fabricated results.
    - Provide accessible model, horizon, metric, plot, and download controls.

validator:
  role: Independent Validator
  goal: Read-only verification of methodology, software behavior, evidence, and repository safety.
  responsibilities:
    - Never modify repository files.
    - Return PASS or FAIL as the first line.
    - For FAIL include exact REQUIRED_CORRECTIONS.
    - Fail when evidence is insufficient or output is malformed.
===== orchestration/config/tasks.yaml =====
implementation:
  description: |
    Implement phase "{phase_name}" as the {specialist_role}.
    Attempt {attempt} of {max_attempts}.
    Read all repository governance documents and the {specialist_role} profile.
    Run relevant tests and checks. Preserve useful evidence.
    Do not advance phases, invoke the validator, push, scrape, acquire Indian-city
    data, alter approved ML methodology, or use danger-full-access.
    If completion requires an action listed under PERMISSIONS.md "Must Ask User
    First", make no such change and return PERMISSION_REQUIRED on the first line,
    followed by the exact approval needed.
  expected_output: A concise implementation summary with changed files and checks run.

repair:
  description: |
    Repair phase "{phase_name}" as the {specialist_role}.
    Attempt {attempt} of {max_attempts}.
    The independent validator returned this exact report:

    {validation_report}

    Apply every REQUIRED_CORRECTION without changing unrelated code or approved
    methodology. Re-run relevant tests and report the changes and evidence.
    If a correction requires user approval under PERMISSIONS.md, make no such
    change and return PERMISSION_REQUIRED followed by the exact approval needed.
  expected_output: A concise repair summary mapping changes to every required correction.

validation:
  description: |
    Independently validate phase "{phase_name}" using read-only access.
    Treat the implementation summary only as a claim to verify:

    {implementation_summary}

    Return PASS or FAIL on the first line. If FAIL, include REQUIRED_CORRECTIONS
    with exact corrections. Do not modify any repository file.
  expected_output: A strict PASS/FAIL validation report with evidence.

